movenc: audio pre-roll sample group in fragments

A decoder that starts on a fragment of an audio track with seek pre-roll
needs to know that the first samples' output wants the packets before
them. Apple's HLS writer states it as a fragment-local sample group of
grouping type 'prol'; movenc writes the roll group of Opus and AAC only in
the sample table of an unfragmented file.

With the new movflags value frag_preroll each traf of an audio track whose
codec parameters carry seek_preroll and frame_size, and that holds a
sample which is not a sync sample, gets after its tfdt:

  sgpd  version 1, grouping type 'prol', default_length 2, one entry:
        roll_distance = seek_preroll / frame_size, rounded up
  sbgp  version 0, grouping type 'prol', one run per change of sync
        status: group_description_index 0x10001 (the first entry of this
        fragment's sgpd) for the samples that are not sync samples, 0 for
        sync samples

A fragment of sync samples only gets neither box. The moof size pass
accounts for the boxes, so trun data offsets stay right. Without the flag
the output is unchanged, so stream-copied Opus, which carries
seek_preroll, is not affected.

--- a/libavformat/movenc.c
+++ b/libavformat/movenc.c
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@
